## Solution

Let $f \in \mathcal{F}$, so $f:\mathbb{D}\to\mathbb{D}$ is holomorphic with $f(0)=f'(0)=f''(0)=f'''(0)=0$.

### Iterated Schwarz Lemma

Since $f(0)=0$ and $|f(z)|<1$ on $\mathbb{D}$, the Schwarz lemma gives $|f(z)|\le|z|$, and $\varphi_1(z):=f(z)/z$ (with $\varphi_1(0)=f'(0)=0$) is holomorphic $\mathbb{D}\to\overline{\mathbb{D}}$.

Now $\varphi_1(0)=0$, so applying Schwarz again: $|\varphi_1(z)|\le|z|$, and $\varphi_2(z):=\varphi_1(z)/z$ (with $\varphi_2(0)=\varphi_1'(0)=f''(0)/2=0$) is holomorphic $\mathbb{D}\to\overline{\mathbb{D}}$.

Again $\varphi_2(0)=0$: $|\varphi_2(z)|\le|z|$, and $\varphi_3(z):=\varphi_2(z)/z$ (with $\varphi_3(0)=\varphi_2'(0)=f'''(0)/6=0$) is holomorphic $\mathbb{D}\to\overline{\mathbb{D}}$.

Once more $\varphi_3(0)=0$: $|\varphi_3(z)|\le|z|$, and $\varphi_4(z):=\varphi_3(z)/z$ (with $\varphi_4(0)=\varphi_3'(0)=f^{(4)}(0)/24$, generally nonzero) is holomorphic $\mathbb{D}\to\overline{\mathbb{D}}$.

### Bounding $|f(1/2)|$

Since $\varphi_4(z) = f(z)/z^4$, we have $f(z)=z^4\varphi_4(z)$ with $|\varphi_4(z)|\le 1$ on $\mathbb{D}$. Therefore

$$|f(1/2)| = \frac{1}{16}\,|\varphi_4(1/2)| \le \frac{1}{16}.$$

### The bound is attained

The function $f(z)=z^4$ maps $\mathbb{D}$ to $\mathbb{D}$, satisfies $f(0)=f'(0)=f''(0)=f'''(0)=0$, and gives $|f(1/2)|=1/16$ (here $\varphi_4\equiv 1$). Hence the supremum is achieved.

$$\sup_{f\in\mathcal{F}}|f(1/2)| = \boxed{\dfrac{1}{16}}.$$

